menu "Mate Test Seed"

    config MATE_TEST_SEED_NVS_ON_BOOT
        bool "Seed NVS with test WiFi/MQTT credentials on boot, then halt"
        default n
        help
            For hardware testing only. When enabled, app_main() runs
            cmp_test_seed_run() instead of the normal cmp_main_launcher():
            it writes a fixed set of WiFi STA credentials and MQTT broker
            settings into the "mate" NVS namespace (the same one the real
            app reads via the preloaded/wifi repositories), then halts.

            The NVS partition is untouched by a normal `idf.py flash` (only
            bootloader/partition-table/app regions are written), so the
            workflow is: build+flash this seed variant once, let it run to
            completion, then reflash the normal firmware - it will boot
            with the seeded credentials already in NVS.

            Never enable this for a real deployment build.

endmenu
